<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Tripoli</h1><p class="st-meta">1102 CE – 1289 CE · capital Tripoli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Crusader state to be founded, a Lebanese coastal county that held Krak des Chevaliers and lasted until 1289.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-iv-of-toulouse">Raymond of Saint-Gilles</a>, count of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a>, besieged Tripoli from 1102, building the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-pilgrim">Mount Pilgrim</a> outside the city, but died in 1105. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-of-toulouse">Bertrand</a> took the city from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banu-ammar-of-tripoli">Banu Ammar</a> in July 1109, and the county was formed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county ran along the coast from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Jubail</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartus">Tortosa</a> and inland to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes</a>. Its counts, from the house of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a>, gave the Hospitallers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krak-des-chevaliers">Krak des Chevaliers</a> in 1142, and the military orders came to hold much of the frontier. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-iii-of-tripoli">Raymond III</a> was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in the 1170s and 1180s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and paper industries continued under Frankish rule. From the early 13th century the county was united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-antioch">Principality of Antioch</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krak-des-chevaliers">Krak des Chevaliers</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> in 1271. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalawun">Qalawun</a> stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a> in April 1289, and a new city was built inland.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-tripoli.jpg" alt="County of Tripoli" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_Arms_of_the_House_of_Toulouse-Tripoli.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1102 CE – 1289 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tripoli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Raymond of Saint-Gilles, Bertrand of Toulouse, Raymond III of Tripoli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tripoli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1196&amp;focus=county-of-tripoli" aria-label="County of Tripoli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5591 931 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Tripoli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5911 1187L5911 1187M5911 1187L5911 1127M5911 1187L5908 1277M5911 1187L5815 1335"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5911 1187h0M5911 1127h0M5908 1277h0M5815 1335h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5911 1187h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5911 1187h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tripoli. <a href="/atlas?year=1196&amp;focus=county-of-tripoli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

